From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Onyx contributors <onyx@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:33:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] WebCrypto with USE(MBEDTLS): the key containers, the
 digests; the rest not implemented yet

What: crypto/keys/CryptoKeyEC.h, CryptoKeyRSA.h: the platform key container for USE(MBEDTLS)
(crypto/mbedtls/MbedTLSCryptoUniquePtr.h: an owned mbedtls_pk_context).
crypto/mbedtls/CryptoAlgorithmRegistryMbedTLS.cpp registers SHA-1 / 256 / 384 / 512 only (they
run on PAL::CryptoDigest). CryptoNotImplementedMbedTLS.cpp defines the platform functions of the
other algorithms and of the RSA / EC keys as "not supported": none of them is registered, so
crypto.subtle answers NotSupportedError for them; they exist for the generic code that names
them.

Why: WebCrypto cannot be switched off and its portable back ends are OpenSSL and gcrypt, which
Onyx does not have. This lets WebCore link; a real back end (on mbedTLS, or OpenSSL's
libcrypto) is still to be decided and written.
